      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:ddq1ux'
    '|a||A third sign: openness. Denmark''s exports and imports come to a hundred and thirty percent of its GDP; America''s to twenty-five. Small countries always trade more, but open is open.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:hkragx'
    '|b||So who does what? Markets decide what gets made and which firms survive. The state taxes, and insures people.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1q7hzq8'
    '|a||People, not firms. In 2009, when Saab was failing, Sweden''s government refused to buy it: taxpayers, said the minister, should not own car factories.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:166ot16'
    '|b||But the people who lose their jobs get income and retraining. A Swedish minister put it this way: we won''t protect jobs, but we will protect workers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:psegwo'
    '|a||Two dials means you can turn one without the other. Give Denmark America''s rules and keep its taxes: its dot rises straight up, and doesn''t move sideways.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1qvrui2'
    '|b||Your turn: find the country with a state as big as Denmark''s, but heavier rules on firms. Tap the country with Denmark''s taxes but heavier rules.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:3ozo9o'
    '|b||Your turn: find the country with a state as big as Denmark''s, but heavier rules on firms.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||France: taxes as high as Denmark''s, and heavier rules on firms than any Nordic country.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||Want the number behind ''a little less''? Show the math, or skip it?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||A correlation measures how tightly two things move together, from minus one to plus one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5640
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Across all thirty-eight, tax take and rules on firms correlate at minus zero point four three.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1oozh02'
    '|a||Keep only the nineteen richest, above fifty thousand dollars a head: minus zero point one. Close to nothing.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1fwd83c'
    '|a||So the two dials barely move together: knowing one tells you little about the other.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1m4ule1'
    '|a||So a big state and free markets can live side by side. But has the mix always worked? Follow Sweden''s tax take since 1965.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||Thirty-one percent of GDP in 1965. Almost forty-nine by 1990.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1kqbz7v'
    '|a||Meanwhile Sweden slid. Fourth richest of twenty-three rich countries in 1970; sixteenth by 1993.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:ojd957'
    '|b||The economist Assar Lindbeck called it the Swedish experiment: high taxes, heavy rules, and subsidies for ailing firms. A banking crisis in the early nineties ended it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10960
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:12z313p'
    '|a||Then Sweden re-tuned: vouchers for private schools, competition in telecoms and electricity, a new pension system, a cap on spending. Taxes peaked at fifty percent in 2000, and have drifted down to forty-two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1v2si07'
    '|b||So the mix that works today is a tuned one, with more room for markets than in 1990.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:jppenq'
    '|a||Two more doubts. Nima Sanandaji argues the Nordics were trusting, hard-working and fairly equal before the big state, so the state may get credit it hasn''t earned.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ndatmx'
    '|b||And Acemoglu, Robinson and Verdier ask whether cuddly Nordic capitalism lives off cutthroat America''s risky inventions. Critics answer that the Nordics invent plenty themselves.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11680
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1gkkpae'
    '|a||How sure are we? That a big state can sit beside open, lightly regulated markets is mostly agreed: the Nordics show it can.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:84cvn'
    '|b||Whether the mix causes their success, and whether it would travel to a bigger, less trusting country, is contested.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow #ctx:1rqt8jr'
    '|a||Its strength: markets pick the winners while the state shares the risk. Its weakness: it leans on trust, high employment and a willingness to pay, and no law can order those up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:10pwydd'
    '|a||Three new cases. A country copies Nordic-sized public services but keeps price controls and state-run firms everywhere. Where does it sit on the two dials?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy #ctx:1ouveh1'
    '|a||Big state, heavy rules: the taxes set one dial, the price controls and state firms the other.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|b||A country has light rules on firms, a tax take of 25% of GDP and no unemployment insurance. A big employer fails. Who carries most of the loss?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12400
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|b||The laid-off workers: light rules let the firm fail, and a small state leaves the risk with them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Kore | sharp, friendly co-host: asks what a smart listener would, pushes back with real objections, sometimes explains; dry wit, never exaggerated; brisk lively pace, never slow'
    '|a||A country raises its tax take from 30% to 45% of GDP and, at the same time, scraps most price controls and state monopolies. Where does its dot move on the two dials?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||Right and down: a bigger state on one dial, lighter rules on the other.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: gemini:Achird | curious, open-minded economist host who loves a puzzle; warm, thinks aloud, brisk lively pace (never slow, never rushed); takes objections seriously, never preachy
    '|a||So can markets and states mix well? Yes, when each does what it''s good at. Market or state was never one dial.':
      mp3: 
